                {principle.title}
              <p className="text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground md:col-span-6 md:col-start-7">
                {principle.body}
          ))}

      <section aria-labelledby="classification-title" className="grid gap-12 border-y border-border bg-surface py-16 md:grid-cols-12 md:py-20">
        <div className="md:col-span-5">
          <p className="text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide text-primary">A shared vocabulary
          <h2 className="mt-4 font-heading text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground" id="classification-title">
            Every decision declares what kind of decision it is.
          <p className="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
            The classification prevents today’s provider or file layout from becoming tomorrow’s accidental architecture.
        <dl className="divide-y divide-border border-y border-border md:col-span-6 md:col-start-7">
          <div className="py-5">
            <dt className="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Core
            <dd className="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">Present in every DarkFactory project and changed only through an explicit architecture decision.
          <div className="py-5">
            <dt className="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Capability
            <dd className="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">Optional, intentionally enabled, and removable through a declared manifest and adapter boundary.
          <div className="py-5">
